      "reason": "The experiment is accepted because the fine-tuned model achieves an accuracy of 84.375% on the GSM8K dev set, significantly exceeding the baseline of 75.0%. The training loss shows a healthy convergence pattern, decreasing from ~0.5 to ~0.13 with stable evaluation loss, indicating effective learning without severe overfitting. Analysis of error samples reveals that while the model handles standard arithmetic well, it struggles with complex percentage reversals and multi-step logic involving 'ruined' or 'leftover' items, suggesting that future iterations could benefit from a slightly higher learning rate or more diverse training data covering these specific reasoning patterns to further improve generalization.",
